commit_sha":"754e96c3c599407c5ae39a1d4898dfad0e32c2fa","position":"1786160241608281001-b2989915-da74-4cc2-ba43-cb01dcdb5edd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786160111091218001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4032fb8e-9d40-4158-9e81-a6a711e3996e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"},{"link_uuid":"03de84f6-f040-43a9-a899-9d132f38ffe3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1734-7c6d-5a6a-48fd"},{"link_uuid":"aff0b750-fda0-4e35-864d-248e01f6abdb","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d19d-7f60-0137-475a"},{"link_uuid":"2d332a71-840d-40e1-bdf7-396ca4aa21d4","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"462d-8d84-122a-4812"},{"link_uuid":"b2989915-da74-4cc2-ba43-cb01dcdb5edd","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"67f9-4a07-9667-446a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe multi-project model changes things a reader currently learns from the docs as single-project\nfacts: `docs/jira-sync-setup.md:74` presents `project` as one config line and has no section on\nmultiple projects, `docs/config.md:216-260` documents the `[jira]` block as a single scalar project,\nand `docs/migrations.md` describes the ensure registry without the two units this epic adds. A user\nupgrading a client store also needs to know what the new `required_capabilities` entry means for\nolder binaries in their fleet. None of that is documented by the implementation stories, which own\ncode and tests only.\n\n## Approach\n\nDocument the shipped behaviour and record the architectural decision. The ADR is warranted rather\nthan decorative because two decisions here are load-bearing, non-obvious, and expensive to reverse:\nthat the project set is a property of the **store** rather than of a repo, and that the legacy\nmigration writes **no ticket events**. Both were chosen against plausible alternatives — per-repo\nproject lists and an EDIT-per-ticket backfill — and a future reader who does not know why will be\ntempted back toward them.\n\nThe ADR is `docs/adr/0062-*` — the next number after `0061-measurement-provenance-in-attested-evidence.md`.\nIt records the shared-`prev_snapshot` reasoning for store ownership, the short-lock-budget reasoning\nfor the event-free migration, and the conditional-stamp reasoning for compatibility. It also notes the\nrelationship to ADR 0060, whose churn constraint the mapping satisfies by construction.\n\nDocumentation updates cover the mapping and its `bridge projects` verb, the tri-state project field,\nthe repos field, the two ensure units, and the upgrade note for fleets running mixed binary versions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/adr/0062-many-to-many-tracker-projects.md` (new)\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- `docs/config.md`\n- `docs/migrations.md`\n- `docs/user-guide.md`\n- `docs/ticket-model.md`\n\n## Testing\n\nNo `## Testing` section beyond this note: this story adds no testable behaviour — it is\ndocumentation and an ADR, which `rebar explain plan` names as a legitimately test-free change class.\nVerification is by the repository's existing documentation gates rather than by new tests, and the\nacceptance criteria below name the command that checks each claim.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0062-many-to-many-tracker-projects.md` exists and records the store-ownership,\n      event-free-migration, and conditional-stamp decisions with their rejected alternatives; checked\n      by reading the file and confirming each of the three decisions names what it was chosen over.\n- [ ] The Jira sync and config docs describe the project mapping and no longer present a single\n      scalar project as the only option; checked by confirming no remaining passage states the\n      single-project constraint as current behaviour.\n- [ ] `docs/migrations.md` lists both new ensure units alongside the existing built-ins; checked by\n      confirming each registered id appears in the doc.\n- [ ] The docs state what the `multi-project-bridge` capability means for an older binary and what an\n      operator does about it; checked by confirming the upgrade note names both the fail-closed\n      behaviour and the remedy.\n- [ ] The generated CLI reference includes `bridge projects`; checked by running the repository's\n      documentation generation and confirming the verb appears without a manual edit.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0062-many-to-many-tracker-projects.md","reason":"record store ownership, event-free migration, conditional stamp"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"replace the single-project setup with the project mapping"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"describe the mapping and the per-repo default"},{"path":"docs/migrations.md","reason":"list the two new ensure units"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"document bridge projects and the upgrade note"},{"path":"docs/ticket-model.md","reason":"document the tri-state project field and repos"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","1734-7c6d-5a6a-48fd"],["depends_on","462d-8d84-122a-4812"],["depends_on","67f9-4a07-9667-446a"],["depends_on","cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"],["depends_on","d19d-7f60-0137-475a"],["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7032-d9f3-ed89-4f7b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Document the multi-project model and record ADR 0062","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["47e054f5-0528-4d4f-ba20-37b252701470","5f3d8f29-f51e-4ce5-81c7-b5066861bc5b","4032fb8e-9d40-4158-9e81-a6a711e3996e","03de84f6-f040-43a9-a899-9d132f38ffe3","aff0b750-fda0-4e35-864d-248e01f6abdb","2d332a71-840d-40e1-bdf7-396ca4aa21d4","b2989915-da74-4cc2-ba43-cb01dcdb5edd"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659618625357001,"uuid":"002d6863-8637-411d-a6fb-5fc55edda42f"}